        ":question/id": "0721a79b-46f6-56dc-93df-e0a639013e16",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-49097",
        ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{9x}.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we apply the constant factor rule and take the coefficient $\\frac{1}{9}$ out of the integral. Then we compute the integral of $\\frac{1}{x},$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{9x} & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}ln\u2061|x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
