        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-29838",
        ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we apply the constant factor rule and take the coefficient $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ out of the integral. Then we compute the integral of $\\frac{1}{x},$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
