        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we apply the constant factor rule and take the coefficient $-\\frac{2}{5}$ out of the integral. Then we compute the integral of $\\frac{1}{x},$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int -\\frac{2}{5x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{2}{5}\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{5}ln\u2061|x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
